WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.690
The stage's evidence supports impact
analysis and contingency planning for the

2
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.915
preflight, configuration change control
for the plans and the ring exits,

3
00:00:08.915 --> 00:00:11.754
the contingency plan for
the rehearsed rollback,

4
00:00:11.754 --> 00:00:14.663
and protection of audit
information for the chain.

5
00:00:14.663 --> 00:00:16.825
The assessor decides the controls.

6
00:00:16.825 --> 00:00:20.000
The dangers: changing a
ring before its logs exist,

7
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.943
a policy that catches
the emergency accounts,

8
00:00:22.943 --> 00:00:27.666
a plan applied that differs from the
one reviewed, an improvised rollback,

9
00:00:27.666 --> 00:00:30.841
production before the test
evidence is complete,

10
00:00:30.841 --> 00:00:33.087
and unattended runs of the beta API.

11
00:00:33.087 --> 00:00:36.934
You're done when every stage's
preflight passed, the rollback was

12
00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:40.999
reviewed and rehearsed, and every
hash was approved by someone else.

13
00:00:40.999 --> 00:00:44.062
That's the end of Building
Global Secure Access.

14
00:00:44.062 --> 00:00:45.220
Thanks for watching.
